  "slug": "machine-learning-assisted-83b8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a publication present installable tools for nucleic acid reagent design, with BaitBench adding built-in assessment and thermodynamic…",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational design of nucleic acid reagents delivered as installable software. BaitBench, a Rust tool with CLI and GUI access, unifies hybrid capture probe design, assessment and thermodynamic simulation, and reports a correlation of rho=0.916 in its evaluation. PoolParty, a Python package, represents oligo pool DNA libraries as computational graphs, offering more than 50 mutagenesis, motif and barcode operations alongside design cards. What is new is the combination of design and in silico evaluation within a single tool, as in BaitBench. The remaining items, including FastaGuard, DoAggregate, NBDC Data Tools and gcat/its_a_scam, address analysis and quality-control infrastructure rather than reagent design and do not share this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
